<string name="keys_text"><![CDATA[
<h3>SELECTING FILES</h3>
<p>
To select files and folders, tap to the <b>right</b> of their rows and open them by tapping to the <b>left</b>.
That\'s right, one side will activate items and the other one will select them.
</p>
<h3>COPYING AND MOVING</h3>
<p>
Copy or move files and folders by first choosing the target destination in one panel, then swipe (or toggle) back to the other panel and select the items you wish to transfer. Then commit the desired operation.
</p>
<h3>EXTERNAL CARDS AND USB OTG</h3>
<p>
On devices with Android 11 (R) on newer, you will be asked to enable the Ghost Commander app to manage all files in the system settings.
After that\'s done, files on the external volumes (such as USB OTG) should be fully accessible in the native mode.
</p>
<h3>ZIP FILES</h3>
<p>
Ghost Commander can handle ZIP archives as if they were
folders. Other archive types are not supported.
</p>
<h3>LOCATION EDITOR</h3>
<p>
To enter a location manually (and to see a drop-down list of your
favorites), long-press the panel\'s header to open the location
editor.\n
You can enter resource URIs into the location editor manually as
follows:
</p><p>
<b>ftp://</b><i>host.com</i><b>/</b><i>folder</i><br/>
- Anonymous FTP
</p><p>
<b>ftp://</b><i>user</i><b>:</b><i>pass</i><b>@</b><i>ftp_host</i><b>/</b><i>folder</i><br/>
- Authenticated FTP
</p><p>
<b>sftp://</b><i>user</i><b>:</b><i>pass</i><b>@</b><i>sftp_host</i><b>/</b><i>folder</i><br/>
- SSH FTP <br/>
If you have a private authentication key file, you will need to load it to the SFTP Keys Manger.
For that, tap and hold on the SFTP item in the \"home:\" screen, then choose \"Settings\" -> \"PEM Keys manager\".
Set your key name as the exact host name you are planning to connect to.
In the case of the key authentication, the user password will be the passphrase to your key file.<br/>
If you need to login to the same server as two or more different users, set the key name
in the format user@host<br/>
Having more than one key per an account is not supported.
</p><p>
A standard <a href="https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man5/ssh_config.5.html">ssh_config</a>
 file could be used for fine tuning the sftp. If the file /sdcard/.GhostCommander/ssh_config exists
its lines will be parsed and applied to the client configuration.
(However, not all options are supported)
</p><p>
<b>smb://</b><i>domain</i><b>;</b><i>user</i><b>:</b><i>pass</i><b>@</b><i>server</i><b>/</b><i>share</i><br/>
- Windows share
</p><p>
<b>root:/</b><i>path/to/folder</i><br/>
- Root mode<br/>
Using the root mode (superuser) features of Ghost
Commander require caution, and will only work on a rooted device.
Also, BusyBox should be installed with its path defined in the settings.<br/>
To show the root item in the \"home:\" screen, enable such option in the app settings.
</p>
<h3>PLUGINS</h3>
<p>
Plugins, which have to be installed separately, provide access to
Box, Dropbox as well as any cloud service which supports WebDAV.
</p>
<h3>HOT KEYS</h3>
<p>(For devices with a keyboard)<br/>
<b><i>VolumeUp</i></b> - Select files and folders<br/>
<b><i>VolumeDn</i></b> - Toggle between the panels<br/>
<b>1</b> - Help<br/>
<b>2</b> - Rename selected item<br/>
<b>4</b> - Edit selected item<br/>
<b>5</b> - Copy selected item(s)<br/>
<b>6</b> - Move selected item(s)<br/>
<b>7</b> - Create a new folder<br/>
<b>8</b> - Delete selected item(s)<br/>
<b>9</b> - Open preferences/settings<br/>
<b>0</b> - Close the app<br/>
<b>[A-z]</b> - Quick search<br/>
<b>/</b> - File search<br/>
<b>&amp;</b> - File filter<br/>
<b>+</b>, <b>-</b> - Select or unselect items in the current folder<br/>
<b>(</b>, <b>)</b> - Enter a location manually and view your favorites<br/>
<b>*</b> - Add the current folder to your favorites<br/>
<b>\"</b> - Show detailed information for the selected item(s)<br/>
<b>=</b> - Display the same location in the other panel (synchronize)<br/>
</p>
<p>
<a href="https://sites.google.com/site/ghostcommander1/info">More help online…</a>
</p>
